IO-47: carry the groundwater table and soil moisture through a runoff interface file

RunoffInterfaceFile wrote 0 for the groundwater elevation and upper-zone soil
moisture of every subcatchment and skipped both on reading, so a USE RUNOFF
run reported the initial water table and moisture for the whole run, and a
legacy run reading a 6.0.0 file got a water table at the aquifer bottom. Pass
the groundwater state to saveResults()/readResults(): write
(bottom_elev + lower_depth) * UCF(LENGTH) and theta as legacy
subcatch_getResults() does, and restore lower_depth and theta from them.

Requires: IO-45
Requires: IO-46

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-45_swmm600.patch IO-46_swmm600.patch IO-47_swmm600.patch

